// A shell block runs its commands on the host, and a host escape `$( … )`
// hands a gandr string to a command as one argument, its spaces kept. The
// lowering admits no shell block yet (#1057).

/// `printf` handed one argument with spaces through a host escape (#1057).
@[ refuses("OutOfFragment.shell_block") ]
#!{
  printf 'hello from the host\n<%s>\n' $("one argv with spaces");
}
